{"step_index":97,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-09T15:13:31Z","content":"The dated recommendation and handoff review for the export feedback follow-through has been completed and written to [`/workspace/work/decision.md`](file:///workspace/work/decision.md).\n\n### Summary of Key Findings & Recommendation\n\n1. **Do Not Close the Support Tickets:**\n   - The assumption in [`current.md`](file:///workspace/product/current.md) that open tickets might predate rollout is refuted by [`record-b851997b7c.json`](file:///workspace/product/history/support/record-b851997b7c.json), where `age_days: 14` is explicitly defined as `days since async-export rollout`, not ticket age.\n   - Ticket `record-339725ec76` was submitted on `2026-09-06T14:31:00Z` (12 days post-rollout). Ticket `record-f10fee8e5d` has an unknown submission date (`submitted_at: null`, preserved as unknown) and was imported `2026-09-07T18:00:00Z`.\n2. **Underlying Issues Confirmed by Production Telemetry:**\n   - **Signed URL Expiration (>15 min):** In [`record-eb2ad86fcb.json`](file:///workspace/product/history/evidence/record-eb2ad86fcb.json), a 1.8M row CSV export completed in 1,184s (~20 min), but the signed URL was minted at job creation with a 900s (15 min) TTL ([`record-7c21733985.md`](file:///workspace/product/history/actions/record-7c21733985.md)), resulting in HTTP 403.\n   - **Missing Rows on Resumption:** In [`record-6a8741fe3b.json`](file:///workspace/product/history/evidence/record-6a8741fe3b.json), a 2.1M row NDJSON export lost 60,559 records ($2,039,441$ output vs $2,100,000$ expected) accompanied by the warning `\"account relation scan resumed after cursor checkpoint\"`. The September 7 parity fix ([`record-d46f9580f1.md`](file:///workspace/product/history/evidence/record-d46f9580f1.md)) applied only to US CSV under 100k rows and explicitly excluded NDJSON and this run.\n   - The September 5 release ([`record-58a6ae3a8b.md`](file:///workspace/product/history/releases/record-58a6ae3a8b.md)) only adjusted spinner copy without altering worker or URL mechanics.\n3. **Next Actions:**\n   - Keep support tickets open and document true rollout age definitions for Support.\n   - Shift signed URL generation to worker completion or on-demand download request.\n   - Fix cursor checkpoint resumption in account relation scans to eliminate record skipping.\n   - Expand automated test fixtures to include 1M+ and 2M+ row workloads covering long durations and multi-checkpoint resumptions.\n\nFor the complete analysis, telemetry citations, and uncertainties, please inspect [`/workspace/work/decision.md`](file:///workspace/work/decision.md).","thinking":"**Verifying task requirements**\n\nThe request mandates using a specific file for the handoff review. It also requires continuing the export feedback follow-through, addressing reported issues of missing rows and export duration. The product workspace context has been provided. All requirements appear to be met.\n\n\n"}
